Emphasize openness and uniformity of Government-wide CyberSecurity practice

When it comes to CyberSecurity and protecting CUI we must return to the original goals of openness and uniformity. To address uniformity the Department of Defense has authorized the creation of the Cybersecurity Maturation Model Certification program. 

This system will train third party companies to assess the cyber hygiene of companies that touch federal contract information (FCI), which is data generated by the Government not for public release and CUI, which can be generated by or for the government. These third party assessors use a shared assessment methodology NIST Special Publication 800-171a

All other federal agencies, like the DoD, need to consider how they will emphasize the openness and uniformity of protecting CUI. The 171 standards and the assessment methodology make the logical choice for a shared government wide process.

CUI and 171 in Higher Education

In fact in 2021, Federal Student Aid, an Office of the Department of Education will conduct a self assessment of Institutes of Higher Education to  measure readiness to comply with the 32 CFR Part 2002 CUI requirements.

Consider how much critical personal identifiable data flows through the financial aid offices. Information criminals could and do use to siphon billions from the US. Economy. Our student aid data needs protection. It is  Controlled Unclassified Information.

FSA does not need to adopt CMMC. Department of Defense chose to rely on a certification and third party assessment to ensure their 300,000 contractors meet the CUI requirements of 32 CFR Part 2002. This approach may not make sense for the deployment of 171 across the Government but the CyberSecurity methodology should remain the same. A uniform approach strengthens our pipeline and our readiness.  

As a nation we created Controlled Unclassified Information to make sure we share data so 9/11 will never happen again. Today we realize we must secure CUI or we could face devastating attacks that overshadow the tradegy of the Towers falling. 
